  "reasoning": "The prosecution established that the accused, a former employee familiar with the key location, was seen entering the shop after hours by PW-2. Although DW-1 provided an alibi, PW-2's identification under a working street light remains credible. The circumstantial evidence forms a complete chain pointing solely to the guilt of the accused.",
  "legal_standard_applied": "The prosecution must prove every element of the offence beyond reasonable doubt, and where the evidence is circumstantial, the circumstances must form a complete chain consistent only with guilt.",
